; Two patios of the same shape, drawn once, with the shots taken on them held
; nowhere near here.
;
; Neither node says what the ground does, and neither says how well anybody knows
; it. Both are derived from the shots inside the region every time somebody asks,
; and are written into no file a walk would read
; (docs/decisions/0009-derived-values-are-never-written-back.md).
;
; The house wall runs along the north boundary of each, at y = 6, and the ground
; falls away from it towards the garden. The decision the gate turns on is the
; fall from the threshold at (3.5, 5) to the drain edge at (3.5, 1) — four metres
; of run, and fifty millimetres of drop if the patio was laid to the one in
; eighty it was specified at.


